  "intro": "Charles Schwab, Fidelity, Interactive Brokers, Firstrade and tastytrade are five Webull alternatives for stock and options trading. Published prices are $0 for online stock and exchange-traded fund (ETF) trades across all five brokerages, using IBKR Lite at Interactive Brokers, while options contract charges range from $0 at Firstrade to $0.65 per contract at Charles Schwab, with contract fees also applying at Fidelity. [Webull](https://www.webull.com/pricing) lists $0 commissions on United States (US) listed stocks, ETFs and standard options, along with a $0.50 per contract fee on certain index options.\n\nAt The Modern Wallet, we show the math, name what moves it, and explain the tradeoff across published brokerage fee schedules. Webull lists no deposit minimums and passes through regulatory fees, including a Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) fee of $0.0000206 times trade volume, while charging $75 for an outgoing stock transfer.\n\nTo view broader investing resources on this site, explore our [best investment apps for beginners roundup](/roundup/best-investment-apps-for-beginners/) and our [best brokers for treasury bonds roundup](/roundup/best-brokers-for-treasury-bonds/). For detailed fee structures, read our guide on [what do brokers charge to trade](/guides/what-do-brokers-charge-to-trade/), review our [Robinhood alternatives](/alternatives/robinhood/) guide, or check our [Fidelity alternatives](/alternatives/fidelity/) page and the [comparison hub](/compare/).",
